{"success": true, "message": "Test details sent successfully", "data": {"test": {"_id": "69de21e97e39d99b57bc5a93", "analysisVideoCdn": "yt", "exam": ["605dfcb2f226ac25a8bd5fef"], "ctype": null, "position": 0, "order": 12, "enableCalculator": false, "isContinuousQuestion": false, "reattemptAvailable": false, "singleSectionMultipleSubjects": false, "timeRestricted": false, "title": "Motion in Two Dimensions - Test 2", "description": "Previous Year Questions as Chapter Test", "syllabus": "This test contains questions from all topics of this chapter included in the JEE Main syllabus. It includes a mix of questions from PYQs of JEE Main 2019 - 2025.", "totalTime": 50, "totalQuestions": 25, "totalMarks": 100, "bonusQuestions": null, "bonusMarks": null, "startDate": "2026-04-15T03:30:00.000Z", "endDate": "2027-04-30T00:00:00.000Z", "type": "free", "class": "605df635a37b7025c438d685", "instruction": "608289ffb160b022e9442c83", "subjects": [{"subjectId": "607018ee404ae53194e73d90", "totalMarks": 100, "bonusMarks": 0, "totalQuestions": 25, "bonusQuestions": 0, "_id": "69de4f212ee0e063d9240393"}], "sections": [{"sectionId": {"_id": "69de4f212ee0e063d92402b4", "title": "Physics Single Correct", "sectionType": "normal", "subject": "607018ee404ae53194e73d90", "questions": [{"_id": "69de4f212ee0e063d924023b", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df7c"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b476a"], "concepts": ["60e5671a499d1e49588f87c6"], "question": {"text": "A particle is projected with velocity $u$ so that its horizontal range is three times the maximum height attained by it. The horizontal range of the projectile is given as $\\frac{n u^2}{25 g}$, where value of $n$ is : (Given ' $g$ ' is the acceleration due to gravity)."}, "options": [{"id": "e6cdea", "text": "$6$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f212ee0e063d924023c"}, {"id": "3250c3", "text": "$18$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f212ee0e063d924023d"}, {"id": "056f7f", "text": "$12$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f212ee0e063d924023e"}, {"id": "c97b2e", "text": "$24$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f212ee0e063d924023f"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f212ee0e063d9240240", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df7c"], "topics": ["60e5671c499d1e49588f87ff"], "concepts": ["60e56739499d1e49588f8b52"], "question": {"text": "A girl standing on road holds her umbrella at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>45</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math> with the vertical to keep the rain away. If she starts running without umbrella with a speed of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>15</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>km</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>, the rain drops hit her head vertically. The speed of rain drops with respect to the moving girl is"}, "options": [{"id": "0bdbc5", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>km</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f212ee0e063d9240241"}, {"id": "d421e9", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>25</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>km</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f212ee0e063d9240242"}, {"id": "ac8a14", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>30</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>km</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f212ee0e063d9240243"}, {"id": "0010cd", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>25</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>km</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f212ee0e063d9240244"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f212ee0e063d9240245", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df7c"], "topics": ["60e567de499d1e49588f9cd4"], "concepts": ["60e567dc499d1e49588f9ca9"], "question": {"text": "A particle is moving along a circular path with a constant speed of $10 \\mathrm{~ms}^{-1}$. What is the magnitude of the change in velocity of the particle, when it moves through an angle of $60^{\\circ}$ around the centre of the circle?"}, "options": [{"id": "5f33a4", "text": "$10 \\sqrt{3} \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f212ee0e063d9240246"}, {"id": "beb990", "text": "zero", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f212ee0e063d9240247"}, {"id": "8c97c8", "text": "$10 \\sqrt{2} \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f212ee0e063d9240248"}, {"id": "934246", "text": "$10 \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f212ee0e063d9240249"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f212ee0e063d924024a", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df7c"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b476a"], "concepts": ["60e56768499d1e49588f8ed9"], "question": {"text": "Two projectiles are projected at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math> and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>60</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>with the horizontal with the same speed. The ratio of the maximum height attained by the two projectiles respectively is:"}, "options": [{"id": "a1894b", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>:</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f212ee0e063d924024b"}, {"id": "9d6768", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>:</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f212ee0e063d924024c"}, {"id": "977688", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>:</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f212ee0e063d924024d"}, {"id": "bfebdf", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>:</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>3</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f212ee0e063d924024e"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f212ee0e063d924024f", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df7c"], "topics": ["60e567de499d1e49588f9cd4"], "concepts": ["6117b88f67dbe2603c3e8087"], "question": {"text": "A man carrying a monkey on his shoulder does cycling smoothly on a circular track of radius $9 \\mathrm{~m}$ and completes 120 resolutions in 3 minutes. The magnitude of centripetal acceleration of monkey is $\\left(\\right.$ in $\\mathrm{m} / \\mathrm{s}^2$ ) :"}, "options": [{"id": "e8cfd6", "text": "$57600 \\pi^2 \\mathrm{~ms}^{-2}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f212ee0e063d9240250"}, {"id": "746940", "text": "Zero", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f212ee0e063d9240251"}, {"id": "1917ec", "text": "$4 \\pi^2 \\mathrm{~ms}^{-2}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f212ee0e063d9240252"}, {"id": "56b6f2", "text": "$16 \\pi^2 \\mathrm{~ms}^{-2}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f212ee0e063d9240253"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f212ee0e063d9240254", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df7c"], "topics": ["60e5671c499d1e49588f87ff"], "concepts": ["60e56813499d1e49588fa38c"], "question": {"text": "<p>A boy reaches the airport and finds that the escalator is not working. He walks up the stationary escalator in time <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;If he remains stationary on a moving escalator then the escalator takes him up in time <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;The time taken by him to walk up on the moving escalator will be:</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "828552", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f212ee0e063d9240255"}, {"id": "91beab", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f212ee0e063d9240256"}, {"id": "936452", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f212ee0e063d9240257"}, {"id": "8fc3d8", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f212ee0e063d9240258"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f212ee0e063d9240259", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df7c"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b476a"], "concepts": ["60e2fad966f9ce3f243b4720"], "question": {"text": "A particle starts from the origin at <math><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> with an initial velocity of <math><mn>3.0</mn><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>^</mo></mover><mi></mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>/</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math> and moves in the <math><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi></math> plane with a constant acceleration <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>6.0</mn><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>4.0</mn><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>/</mo><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>.</mo></math> The <math><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo></math> coordinate of the particle at the instant when its <math><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo></math> coordinate is <math><mn>32</mn><mi></mi><mi>m</mi></math> is <math><mi>D</mi></math> meters. The value of <math><mi>D</mi></math> is:"}, "options": [{"id": "e5931e", "text": "<math><mn>32</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f212ee0e063d924025a"}, {"id": "2a9706", "text": "<math><mn>50</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f212ee0e063d924025b"}, {"id": "33b7f2", "text": "<math><mn>60</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f212ee0e063d924025c"}, {"id": "348974", "text": "<math><mn>40</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f212ee0e063d924025d"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f212ee0e063d924025e", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df7c"], "topics": ["60e567de499d1e49588f9cd4"], "concepts": ["60e567fa499d1e49588fa01d"], "question": {"text": "<p>A clock has a continuously moving second&#39;s hand of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> length. The average acceleration of the tip of the hand (in units of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>ms</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;]) is of the order of :</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "caa1d7", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f212ee0e063d924025f"}, {"id": "a77090", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f212ee0e063d9240260"}, {"id": "855e82", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f212ee0e063d9240261"}, {"id": "2e2ac7", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f212ee0e063d9240262"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f212ee0e063d9240263", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df7c"], "topics": ["60e5671c499d1e49588f87ff"], "concepts": ["60e56813499d1e49588fa38c"], "question": {"text": "A passenger train of length <math><mn>60</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>m</mi></math> travels at a speed of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>80</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>km</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>hr</mi></math>. Another freight train of length <math><mn>120</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>m</mi></math> travels at a speed of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>km</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>hr</mi></math>. The ratio of times taken by the passenger train to completely cross the freight train when: (i) they are moving in the same direction, and (ii) in the opposite directions is:"}, "options": [{"id": "b8ca73", "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f212ee0e063d9240264"}, {"id": "ed9af5", "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f212ee0e063d9240265"}, {"id": "2a3903", "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>11</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f212ee0e063d9240266"}, {"id": "8fb042", "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>25</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>11</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f212ee0e063d9240267"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f212ee0e063d9240268", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df7c"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b476a"], "concepts": ["60e567fa499d1e49588fa019"], "question": {"text": "Two projectiles are fired from ground with same initial speeds from same point at angles $\\left(45^{\\circ}+\\alpha\\right)$ and $\\left(45^{\\circ}-\\alpha\\right)$ with horizontal direction. The ratio of their times of flights is"}, "options": [{"id": "7ca936", "text": "1", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f212ee0e063d9240269"}, {"id": "7a76c4", "text": "$\\frac{1-\\tan \\alpha}{1+\\tan \\alpha}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f212ee0e063d924026a"}, {"id": "97899c", "text": "$\\frac{1+\\sin 2 \\alpha}{1-\\sin 2 \\alpha}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f212ee0e063d924026b"}, {"id": "1107d5", "text": "$\\frac{1+\\tan \\alpha}{1-\\tan \\alpha}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f212ee0e063d924026c"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f212ee0e063d924026d", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df7c"], "topics": ["60e567de499d1e49588f9cd4"], "concepts": ["6176f3f46581241c7072ae6a"], "question": {"text": "A stone of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mi>kg</mi></math> is tied to end of a massless string of length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>. If the breaking tension of the string is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>400</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math>, then maximum linear velocity, the stone can have without breaking the string, while rotating in horizontal plane, is:"}, "options": [{"id": "ee2d70", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f212ee0e063d924026e"}, {"id": "6c83b8", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>40</m