13ed1", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mn>10</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f212ee0e063d924029c"}, {"id": "70ab33", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mn>6</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mn>10</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>12</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f212ee0e063d924029d"}, {"id": "54b709", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f212ee0e063d924029e"}], "questionLabels": []}], "markingScheme": {"_id": "608283e223cf4b3ad8f125e6", "title": "JEE Single Correct", "correctAttempt": 4, "incorrectAttempt": -1, "createdAt": "2021-04-09T08:45:27.797Z", "updatedAt": "2021-07-05T05:39:15.785Z", "__v": 0, "updated_by": "6042252509c5bf34e8a2f178"}, "maximumAttemptLimit": 20, "linkedQuestions": [], "createdAt": "2026-04-14T14:28:49.790Z", "updatedAt": "2026-04-14T14:28:49.790Z", "__v": 0}, "position": 0, "_id": "69de4f212ee0e063d9240391"}, {"sectionId": {"_id": "69de4f212ee0e063d924038f", "title": "Physics Numerical", "sectionType": "normal", "subject": "607018ee404ae53194e73d90", "questions": [{"_id": "69de4f212ee0e063d92402db", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df7c"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b476a"], "concepts": ["617aa9b9ef3fe65ad8e80c77"], "question": {"text": "A body of mass $M$ thrown horizontally with velocity $v$ from the top of the tower of height $H$ touches the ground at a distance of $100 \\mathrm{~m}$ from the foot of the tower. A body of mass $2 \\mathrm{M}$ thrown at a velocity $\\frac{v}{2}$ from the top of the tower of height $4 \\mathrm{H}$ will touch the ground at a distance of _____$\\mathrm{m}$."}, "options": [{"id": "29ba67", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f212ee0e063d92402dc"}, {"id": "332a30", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f212ee0e063d92402dd"}, {"id": "6de45d", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f212ee0e063d92402de"}, {"id": "8e3689", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f212ee0e063d92402df"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f212ee0e063d92402e0", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df7c"], "topics": ["60e5671c499d1e49588f87ff"], "concepts": ["60e5671a499d1e49588f87ca"], "question": {"text": "The speed of a swimmer is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>km</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> in still water. If the swimmer makes his strokes normal to the flow of river of width <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>km</mi></math>, he reaches a point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>750</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> down the stream on the opposite bank. The speed of the river water is ______&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>km</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>."}, "options": [{"id": "23b96a", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f212ee0e063d92402e1"}, {"id": "f7aa70", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f212ee0e063d92402e2"}, {"id": "155e36", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f212ee0e063d92402e3"}, {"id": "91bc12", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f212ee0e063d92402e4"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f212ee0e063d92402e5", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df7c"], "topics": ["60e567de499d1e49588f9cd4"], "concepts": ["6117b98967dbe2603c3ea30c"], "question": {"text": "A car is moving on a circular path of radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>600</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>&nbsp;such that the magnitudes of the tangential acceleration and centripetal acceleration are equal. The time taken by the car to complete first quarter of revolution, if it is moving with an initial speed of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>54</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>km</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#8211;</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>&#8211;</mo><mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi></math> is ______."}, "options": [{"id": "85ee92", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f212ee0e063d92402e6"}, {"id": "d113ca", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f212ee0e063d92402e7"}, {"id": "84b2a3", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f212ee0e063d92402e8"}, {"id": "a023a6", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f212ee0e063d92402e9"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f212ee0e063d92402ea", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df7c"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b476a"], "concepts": ["60e56768499d1e49588f8ed9"], "question": {"text": "A body is projected from the ground at an angle of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>45</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math> with the horizontal. Its velocity after <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. The maximum height reached by the body during its motion is _____&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math>. (use <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>)"}, "options": [{"id": "3b44bd", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f212ee0e063d92402eb"}, {"id": "81ad1a", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f212ee0e063d92402ec"}, {"id": "7d3967", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f212ee0e063d92402ed"}, {"id": "f04fcc", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f212ee0e063d92402ee"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f212ee0e063d92402ef", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df7c"], "topics": ["60e5671c499d1e49588f87ff"], "concepts": ["60e5671a499d1e49588f87ca"], "question": {"text": "<p>A swimmer wants to cross a river from point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;to point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>. Line AB makes an angle of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math> with the flow of the river. The magnitude&nbsp;of the velocity of the swimmer is the same as that of the river. The angle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#952;</mi></math> with the line <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></math> should be _______<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#176;</mo></math>, so that the swimmer reaches point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>.</p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fp